<title>INDONESIA: Indonesia rubber market closed on Friday.</title>
<headline>Indonesia rubber market closed on Friday.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's rubber market was closed on Friday due to the Moslem Eid al-Adha celebration.</p>
<p>Traders said Indonesian tyre-grade SIR20 rubber prices were unchanged in late trading on Thursday as buying interest remained thin with a deal was done at 47.75 U.S. cents/lb in Banjarmasin for July shipment.</p>
<p>They said SIR20 was unchanged on Thursday at 48.50 in Medan. Trading will resume on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
